  "content": "<a href=\"https://burgasmedia.com/?lang=en\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Home</a>\n                                                              /\n              <a href=\"https://burgasmedia.com/category/novinite-na-burgas?lang=en\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Burgas</a>\n                        /\n            Loud boom heard in three Burgas districts, caus...\n          \n\n          \n                          <a href=\"https://burgasmedia.com/category/novinite-na-burgas?lang=en\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Burgas</a>\n            \n                        \n            \n                        \n\n                          \n            \n            \n              <p>Borislav Stanev\n                \n                  26.11.2026 • 17:53                  · 2198 views\n                  · 1 comments\n                \n              </p>\n            \n          \n\n                                  \n          \n          \n                      <p>Residents heard the boom on the morning of 26 November in Slaveykov, Lazur and Vetren. Burgas council and the operator of the quarry near Gorno Ezerovo did not confirm any blasting.</p>\n          \n          \n                                                  \n            <p>A loud boom shook the Slaveykov, Lazur and Vetren districts of Burgas on the morning of 26 November.</p><p>Neither Burgas council nor the operator of the stone quarry near Gorno Ezerovo has publicly confirmed any blasting that day, so the cause of the noise has not been officially established. Residents described the boom in the Facebook group \"Mamite na Burgas\", and more than 40 of them wrote in the comments that a blast at the quarry may have caused it. This is a guess by local people, not confirmed information.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"https://burgasmedia.com/uploads/images/img_6b085602a0b697.05176587.webp\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://burgasmedia.com/uploads/images/img_6b085602a0b697.05176587.webp\" alt=\"A loud boom was heard in three districts of Burgas, the cause has not been announced\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1200\" /></a><figcaption>Photo: Vammpi, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gorno_Ezerovo_Stadion1.JPG\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a></figcaption></figure>\n<p>The quarry has carried out controlled blasts before to break up rock during mining, and an earlier boom from there also alarmed Burgas residents.</p>          \n          \n\n          \n          \n          \n                      \n              <p><img src=\"https://burgasmedia.com/avatar.php?n=%D0%91%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%20%D0%A1%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B2&amp;bg=0F1E3D&amp;s=128\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" /></p>\n                <p><a href=\"https://burgasmedia.com/author/borislav.stanev?lang=en\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Borislav Stanev</strong></a>\n                Author of this article</p><p>Covers Burgas and the region: incidents, crime cases, social policy and civil rights. Follows what happens in the city day by day and which decisions affect people directly. The pieces are prepared with editorial technology and go through editorial review before publication.</p>\n              \n            \n          \n                              \n                              \n          \n          \n                          <p>Tags:\n                                  Burgas\n                                  unexplained noise\n                                  Bulgaria news\n                                  explosion\n                                  loud bang\n                              </p>